// How a Debug build is signed — the Boltty target's Debug configuration.
//
// Ad hoc ("-") unless this Mac has an identity of its own:
// scripts/setup-local-signing.sh writes Signing.local.xcconfig beside this
// file (ignored by git) naming "Boltty Development", the certificate
// `release.sh` signs with when there is no Developer ID.
//
// Why it matters: macOS keeps one privacy grant per bundle id and pins it to
// the code's designated requirement. An ad hoc build's requirement is its own
// hash, so every Xcode build was a new app to the Screen Recording,
// Microphone and Automation grants — and, sharing `com.boltty.app` with the
// copy in /Applications, it took the grant away from that copy too. Signed by
// the same certificate, every build here has the release's requirement
// (`identifier "com.boltty.app" and certificate root = H"…"`) and one grant
// serves them all.
BOLTTY_LOCAL_SIGN_IDENTITY = -
#include? "Signing.local.xcconfig"
